# Era 12 — Navigation & Integration (V40–V42)

_Phase 3 · Concept Layer V1_

**Status: ✅ done, verified 2026-09-17**

**Implementation note:** V40 — the "Concepts" group added to `docs.json`'s Guides tab,
positioned exactly per Era 1 V3's decision (after "Getting started," before "Workflows"),
30/30 pages listed, none missing, none duplicated, `python3 -c "json.load(...)"` confirms
valid JSON. V41 — bidirectional links added: 4 task guides gained an "Understand this
first"/pairing `<Note>` linking to their paired concept page(s) (`deploy-workflow.mdx` ↔
`deployments.mdx`, `scaling.mdx` ↔ `scaling-and-resources.mdx`,
`rollback-and-recovery.mdx` ↔ `rollback-promotion-and-recovery.mdx`,
`connect-and-machine-roles.mdx` ↔ `beaver-cloud.mdx`/`machine-and-agent-operation.mdx`, the
last one found missing during review and added); 36 `cli/*.mdx` reference pages gained a
one-line "New here?" pointer back to their concept page, generated from the concept pages'
own "Next steps" links (not hand-typed, so the pairing can't drift from what each concept
page actually claims to cover) and skipping any page that already had one (idempotent).
V42 — full audit: all 34 topics traced to a real, existing artifact, zero unresolved (see
script output logged in this era's implementation history). `mint broken-links` clean after
every step.

Executes the placement decision fixed in Era 1 V3 and closes every bidirectional-link
obligation Phase 2 deferred to "confirmed at Era 12."

---

## V40 — `docs.json` nav: the new Concepts group

### Goal
Add the "Concepts" group to the Guides tab, positioned per Era 1 V3's decision, populated
with every page Phase 2 produced.

### Reuses
`CLAUDE.md`'s rule that navigation is centrally defined in `docs.json` and pages are not
auto-discovered — same mechanism the sibling roadmap's own Era 12 V41 uses for the CLI tab,
applied here to the Guides tab instead.

### Implement
- Insert a new group object into `docs.json`'s `Guides` tab's `groups` array, positioned
  immediately after `"Getting started"` and before `"Workflows"`:
  ```
  {
    "group": "Concepts",
    "pages": [
      "concepts/how-beaver-fits-together",
      "concepts/accounts-and-workspaces",
      "concepts/integrations",
      "concepts/machine-and-agent-operation",
      "concepts/beaver-cloud",
      "concepts/projects",
      "concepts/configuration",
      "concepts/environments-and-variables",   // only if V16 chose net-new over merge
      "concepts/building-applications",
      "concepts/preflight-and-planning",
      "concepts/deployments",
      "concepts/containers-and-replicas",
      "concepts/compose-applications",
      "concepts/domains-and-routing",
      "concepts/scaling-and-resources",
      "concepts/firewall",
      "concepts/edge-and-performance",
      "concepts/services",
      "concepts/service-databases-and-credentials",
      "concepts/service-clusters",
      "concepts/persistent-storage",
      "concepts/backups-and-restoration",
      "concepts/connecting-to-services-locally",
      "concepts/observability",
      "concepts/state-and-drift",
      "concepts/rollback-promotion-and-recovery",
      "concepts/automation",
      "concepts/troubleshooting",
      "concepts/plans-and-billing"
      // concepts/administrative-commands only if V39 chose (a) over (b)
    ]
  }
  ```
  (Merge-classified topics — Choosing my setup, Installation/CLI basics, Connecting
  machines, Environments and variables if merged — stay in their existing group and are
  **not** duplicated into this list, per Invariant 9.)
- Page files live under a new top-level `concepts/` directory (mirroring `guides/`'s own
  existing pattern), one `.mdx` per page, matching the paths above.

### Validate
Every path in the group array corresponds to a file that exists; no Phase 2 page is missing
from the array; no merge-classified topic appears twice.

### Done when
`docs.json` reflects the final Concepts group and `mint dev` renders it in the correct
sidebar position.

