## V41 — Bidirectional linking

### Goal
Every "confirmed at Era 12" link obligation from Phase 2 is executed: task guides and
reference pages get a link back to their concept page, not just the concept page linking
forward.

### Reuses
The specific pairings named through Phase 2: `guides/deploy-workflow.mdx` ↔
`concepts/deployments.mdx` (V19); `guides/scaling.mdx` ↔ `concepts/scaling-and-resources.mdx`
(V23); `guides/rollback-and-recovery.mdx` ↔ `concepts/rollback-promotion-and-recovery.mdx`
(V34); `guides/connect-and-machine-roles.mdx` ↔ `concepts/beaver-cloud.mdx` /
`machine-and-agent-operation.mdx` (V12/V13); plus every concept page's own "Next steps" link
into whichever `cli/*.mdx` reference page exists at execution time.

### Implement
- Add a short "Understand this first" or "See also" callout (using `<Card>`/`<Note>` per
  `components.txt`) near the top of each named task guide, linking to its paired concept
  page(s).
- For reference pages: add a one-line pointer at the top of each `cli/*.mdx` family page
  this roadmap touches, linking to its concept page — coordinate with `/features/docs/`'s
  own in-progress work so this doesn't collide with that roadmap's own page edits (check
  `eras_implementation.docs` there for what's already landed vs. still in draft before
  editing a shared file).
- Resolve every "reference page may be a placeholder" note logged in Phase 2 (e.g. V9,
  V10) by re-checking whether the sibling roadmap has since published that family; update
  the link or leave the honest placeholder note if not.

### Validate
Spot-check a sample of pairs in both directions; confirm no edit collided with concurrent
work in `/features/docs/`'s reference pages (check git blame/diff before editing shared
files, per this session's own git-safety practice).

### Done when
Every pairing named across Phase 2 is bidirectional; no Phase 2 "confirmed at Era 12" note
remains unresolved.

